## configs/roberta_mnli_apt.yaml
# Logic Analysis for configs/roberta_mnli_apt.yaml
# Purpose:
#   Task-specific override configuration for reproducing APT on RoBERTa-base for MNLI,
#   following the paper "APT: Adaptive Pruning and Tuning Pretrained Language Models for Efficient Training and Inference".
#
# Scope:
#   This file is an override on top of configs/default.yaml and must stay within the
#   ExperimentConfig schema defined in the design. It should not introduce new schema fields
#   beyond what src/config.py is expected to support.
#
# Paper-aligned decisions captured here (from config.yaml + parsed paper):
#   - Backbone: roberta-base
#   - Task: GLUE MNLI (GLUE-big group)
#   - Metric: dev accuracy
#   - APT adapters: attention query/value + FFN layers for small models (RoBERTa)
#   - Distillation: enabled for small models
#   - Hyperparameters (GLUE-big): lr=2e-4, batch_size=32, epochs=40, distill_epochs=20
#   - APT: initial_rank=8, lora scaling factor(alpha)=2, target sparsity=0.60,
#          cubic sparsity schedule, gradual mask update alpha=0.01, outlier-aware kurtosis enabled
#
# MNLI split handling:
#   - Primary validation split: validation_matched
#   - The evaluator/dataset loader may additionally evaluate validation_mismatched if implemented,
#     but this config provides only one validation_split per the design schema.
#
# Inherited/defaulted settings:
